-- Migration 014: QMS clause registry seed (spec 40)
-- Seeds qms.clause_registry (DDL in migration 011) with the tri-standard clause
-- spine: one row per data row of docs/architecture/iso-coverage-matrix.md —
-- ISO9001 (28) + ISO14001 (24) + ISO45001 (28) = 80 rows.
--
-- BC-1: intent_paraphrase is ARCHITECT-AUTHORED paraphrase, adapted from the
--       "(b) Requires:" lines of docs/architecture/iso-requirements-map.md.
--       NO verbatim ISO text is reproduced; clause numbers and titles are
--       factual references only. Paraphrases are present-tense imperative
--       summaries (CLR-3: the ISO modal verb never appears in any paraphrase).
-- BC-7: dedup-narrowed umbrella rows — the ISO14001 6.1 and ISO45001 6.1
--       paraphrases cover ONLY 6.1.1 general + 6.1.4 planning action
--       (environmental aspects, hazards, and legal/compliance obligations live
--       on their own 6.1.2 / 6.1.3 rows); the ISO45001 8.1 paraphrase covers
--       ONLY 8.1.1 general operational planning (8.1.2 / 8.1.3 / 8.1.4 have
--       their own rows). Registry integrity is asserted over PARSED clause
--       numbers against the coverage matrix (qms-registry.test.ts), never a
--       line count.
--
-- UUIDs are deterministic for testability and idempotent re-application:
-- d0000001-000S-4000-8000-0000000000NN (S: 1=ISO9001, 2=ISO14001, 3=ISO45001;
-- NN = document order within the standard section).

-- ============================================================
-- ISO 9001:2015 — 28 rows
-- ============================================================

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- ============================================================
-- ISO 14001:2015 — 24 rows
-- ============================================================

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;

-- ============================================================
-- ISO 45001:2018 — 28 rows
-- ============================================================

ON CONFLICT (id) DO NOTHING;
